# Why not exploitable: Grafana's network exposure is limited to authenticated
# admin users on port 3000 over local host mapping; Loki/Promtail are internal-only.
CVE-2026-33811 exp:2026-08-23

# CVE-2026-34040: Moby authorization bypass.
# Why no fix: Affects promtail v3.6.11 (EOL, no newer tag exists at all) and
# gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:v0.52.1 — re-verified 2026-08-03, checked the newer
# v0.55.1 tag directly, which still carries this (plus a much larger CVE set
# overall, not an improvement).
# Why not exploitable: Promtail does not manage Docker daemon authorization or
# sockets directly in our deployment. cAdvisor is a read-only client of the
# Docker API (container list/inspect/stats only, mounts /var/run read-only) —
# it never runs a Docker daemon or authorization-plugin-gated API of its own,
# so a bypass in that server-side logic isn't triggered by cAdvisor's own code.
CVE-2026-34040 exp:2026-08-23

