# The block below is the Go stdlib / x/crypto / x/net / x/oauth2 DoS and
# parsing-bug backlog from cadvisor's Go 1.24.1 / x-pkg vintage — all
# denial-of-service or memory-safety bugs in HTTP/TLS/HTML/URL parsing paths,
# none of them RCE. Why not exploitable: cadvisor serves only a Prometheus
# metrics scrape endpoint and reads /proc, /sys, and the read-only Docker
# socket — it never parses untrusted HTML or arbitrary URLs, and never
# terminates TLS from an untrusted peer.
# Re-verified 2026-08-03: cadvisor v0.54.1 (45 findings) and v0.55.1 (44) are
# both WORSE than v0.52.1 (43) — each clears 9-10 CVEs but introduces 11.
